      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Identity Chain\nTerraform starts with some credentials, for\nexample the keys of a pipeline. The provider\ncan then assume an IAM role in the target\naccount with `assume_role`, and it can assume\nseveral roles in a row ([role chaining](https:\n//github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/\nblob/v6.73.0/website/docs/index.html.markdown#\nL77)). The final role decides which account\nthe plan touches and what it may do. So read\nthe `role_arn` expression of every provider\nblock. When it depends on the workspace, the\nworkspace picks the account.\n\nTwo settings help. `allowed_account_ids` stops\na run in the wrong account. `default_tags`\nadds the same tags to every resource of the\nprovider ([provider arguments](https://github.\ncom/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.7\n3.0/website/docs/index.html.markdown#L372-L380\n)). The backend that stores the state has its\nown chain, set in the `backend \"s3\"` block.\n\nA configuration can have several provider\nblocks with aliases, for example one for a DNS\naccount and one for the region `us-east-1`. A\nresource then picks its block with `provider =\naws.<alias>`.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-0e46fd6733f9",
      "originalText": "The Identity Chain\nTerraform starts with some credentials, for example the keys of a pipeline. The provider can then assume an IAM role in the target account with `assume_role`, and it can assume several roles in a row ([role chaining](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/index.html.markdown#L77)). The final role decides which account the plan touches and what it may do. So read the `role_arn` expression of every provider block. When it depends on the workspace, the workspace picks the account.\n\nTwo settings help. `allowed_account_ids` stops a run in the wrong account. `default_tags` adds the same tags to every resource of the provider ([provider arguments](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/index.html.markdown#L372-L380)). The backend that stores the state has its own chain, set in the `backend \"s3\"` block.\n\nA configuration can have several provider blocks with aliases, for example one for a DNS account and one for the region `us-east-1`. A resource then picks its block with `provider = aws.<alias>`.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "the-identity-chain"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
