      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "One Document, One Owner\nSeveral AWS settings are a single document\nthat the API replaces as a whole:\n\n- The notification configuration of an S3\nbucket ([notification note](https://github.com\n/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0\n/website/docs/r/s3_bucket_notification.html.ma\nrkdown#L13)).\n- The lifecycle configuration and the policy\nof a bucket.\n- The access policy of an SQS queue or an SNS\ntopic.\n- The inline rules of a security group, which\nis a firewall for network traffic.\n\nIf two resources, or a resource and a person,\nwrite the same document, each write removes\nthe other's part. Plans then show the same\nchange again and again. Give each document\nexactly one owner in Terraform.\n\nSince provider version 4, an S3 bucket has one\nresource for each document:\n`aws_s3_bucket_versioning`,\n`aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration`,\n`aws_s3_bucket_policy`,\n`aws_s3_bucket_notification` and others\n([version 4 upgrade](https://github.com/hashic\norp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/websit\ne/docs/guides/version-4-upgrade.html.markdown#\nL1324-L1335)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-6a9cc2d9f504",
      "originalText": "One Document, One Owner\nSeveral AWS settings are a single document that the API replaces as a whole:\n\n- The notification configuration of an S3 bucket ([notification note](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/r/s3_bucket_notification.html.markdown#L13)).\n- The lifecycle configuration and the policy of a bucket.\n- The access policy of an SQS queue or an SNS topic.\n- The inline rules of a security group, which is a firewall for network traffic.\n\nIf two resources, or a resource and a person, write the same document, each write removes the other's part. Plans then show the same change again and again. Give each document exactly one owner in Terraform.\n\nSince provider version 4, an S3 bucket has one resource for each document: `aws_s3_bucket_versioning`, `aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration`, `aws_s3_bucket_policy`, `aws_s3_bucket_notification` and others ([version 4 upgrade](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/guides/version-4-upgrade.html.markdown#L1324-L1335)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "one-document-one-owner"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
