      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Adders and Owners\nIAM attaches policies to roles. Two styles of\nresource do this:\n\n- Adders add one item and leave the rest\nalone. Examples are\n`aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` and\n`aws_iam_role_policy`.\n- Owners own the whole set and remove items\nthat they do not list. Examples are the\n`inline_policy` and `managed_policy_arns`\narguments of `aws_iam_role` ([role note](https\n://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws\n/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/r/iam_role.html.mar\nkdown#L15)), and the `*_exclusive` resources.\n\nOne owner is a trap.\n`aws_iam_policy_attachment` owns every\nattachment of one policy across the whole\naccount ([warning](https://github.com/hashicor\np/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/\ndocs/r/iam_policy_attachment.html.markdown#L13\n)). If another configuration attaches the same\npolicy elsewhere, the next apply detaches it\nthere. Use `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment`\ninstead.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-68e4efcade69",
      "originalText": "Adders and Owners\nIAM attaches policies to roles. Two styles of resource do this:\n\n- Adders add one item and leave the rest alone. Examples are `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` and `aws_iam_role_policy`.\n- Owners own the whole set and remove items that they do not list. Examples are the `inline_policy` and `managed_policy_arns` arguments of `aws_iam_role` ([role note](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/r/iam_role.html.markdown#L15)), and the `*_exclusive` resources.\n\nOne owner is a trap. `aws_iam_policy_attachment` owns every attachment of one policy across the whole account ([warning](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/r/iam_policy_attachment.html.markdown#L13)). If another configuration attaches the same policy elsewhere, the next apply detaches it there. Use `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` instead.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "adders-and-owners"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
