      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Trust Has Two Sides\nAn IAM role has a trust policy. It names who\nmay assume the role, and it can demand an\nexternal ID, a shared value that the caller\nmust present ([external ID](https://docs.aws.a\nmazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_common\n-scenarios_third-party.html)). Another system\nthat uses the role, such as Snowflake or a\nKafka Connect connector, must know the role's\nARN (Amazon Resource Name, the unique ID of an\nAWS resource) and the external ID. So each\nside needs values from the other side.\n\nWhen the other system generates its values,\nsomeone must copy them into the trust policy,\nfor example in a second apply. When you choose\nthe external ID yourself and fix the role name\nin advance, both sides know every value before\nthe first apply. AWS does not treat the\nexternal ID as a secret. The [Snowflake map](.\n./snowflake/terraform-snowflake.md#two-step-tr\nust-with-aws-two-step-trust-with-aws) shows\nthe three ways that configurations solve this\nloop for Snowflake.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-60b6f75694ff",
      "originalText": "Trust Has Two Sides\nAn IAM role has a trust policy. It names who may assume the role, and it can demand an external ID, a shared value that the caller must present ([external ID](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_common-scenarios_third-party.html)). Another system that uses the role, such as Snowflake or a Kafka Connect connector, must know the role's ARN (Amazon Resource Name, the unique ID of an AWS resource) and the external ID. So each side needs values from the other side.\n\nWhen the other system generates its values, someone must copy them into the trust policy, for example in a second apply. When you choose the external ID yourself and fix the role name in advance, both sides know every value before the first apply. AWS does not treat the external ID as a secret. The [Snowflake map](../snowflake/terraform-snowflake.md#two-step-trust-with-aws-two-step-trust-with-aws) shows the three ways that configurations solve this loop for Snowflake.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "trust-has-two-sides"
      }
    },
