      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Provider Generations\nEach major version of the provider changed how\ncode looks:\n\n| Version | Released | Main change |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4.0.0 | 2022-02-10 | S3 bucket settings\nmoved into separate resources. |\n| 5.0.0 | 2023-05-25 | Tag handling changed,\nand old arguments were removed. |\n| 6.0.0 | 2025-06-18 | Each resource can set\nits own `region`. |\n\nThe upgrade guides list every change ([version\n6 guide](https://github.com/hashicorp/terrafor\nm-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/guide\ns/version-6-upgrade.html.markdown)). HashiCorp\nadvises moving to the latest minor version\nfirst, getting a clean plan, and only then\nraising the major version ([upgrade steps](htt\nps://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-a\nws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/guides/version-6-\nupgrade.html.markdown#L109-L116)).\n\n`awscc` is generated from AWS CloudFormation\nschemas. Every optional attribute in it is\nalso computed, so it cannot detect drift in\nvalues that you did not set, and it ignores\n`default_tags` ([awscc docs](https://github.co\nm/hashicorp/terraform-provider-awscc/blob/v1.1\n10.0/docs/index.md#L20-L26)). HashiCorp built\nit to bring new AWS resources to Terraform\nfaster, and expects it to run next to\n`hashicorp/aws` ([using both providers](https:\n//github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/\nblob/v6.73.0/website/docs/guides/using-aws-wit\nh-awscc-provider.html.markdown)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-c28df3279598",
      "originalText": "Provider Generations\nEach major version of the provider changed how code looks:\n\n| Version | Released | Main change |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4.0.0 | 2022-02-10 | S3 bucket settings moved into separate resources. |\n| 5.0.0 | 2023-05-25 | Tag handling changed, and old arguments were removed. |\n| 6.0.0 | 2025-06-18 | Each resource can set its own `region`. |\n\nThe upgrade guides list every change ([version 6 guide](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/guides/version-6-upgrade.html.markdown)). HashiCorp advises moving to the latest minor version first, getting a clean plan, and only then raising the major version ([upgrade steps](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/guides/version-6-upgrade.html.markdown#L109-L116)).\n\n`awscc` is generated from AWS CloudFormation schemas. Every optional attribute in it is also computed, so it cannot detect drift in values that you did not set, and it ignores `default_tags` ([awscc docs](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-awscc/blob/v1.110.0/docs/index.md#L20-L26)). HashiCorp built it to bring new AWS resources to Terraform faster, and expects it to run next to `hashicorp/aws` ([using both providers](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/guides/using-aws-with-awscc-provider.html.markdown)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "provider-generations"
      }
    },
