      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1454194525,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-e6d94c072290",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1321.2,
      "y": 1940.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 682.5,
      "seed": 94781,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What You Will See\n| Area | Resources | What to check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Data buckets | `aws_s3_bucket`,\n`aws_s3_bucket_versioning`,\n`aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration`,\n`aws_s3_bucket_policy`,\n`aws_s3_bucket_notification`,\n`aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block` |\n`force_destroy`, versioning, expiry rules, one\nnotification resource per bucket |\n| Access | `aws_iam_role`, `aws_iam_policy`,\n`aws_iam_role_policy_attachment`,\n`data.aws_iam_policy_document` | Trust\nprincipals and external IDs, adders or owners\n|\n| Users with keys | `aws_iam_user`,\n`aws_iam_access_key` | Where the secret key\ngoes |\n| Secrets | `aws_secretsmanager_secret`,\n`aws_secretsmanager_secret_version` | Value\nsource, recovery window, `prevent_destroy` |\n| Events | `aws_sns_topic`, `aws_sqs_queue`,\n`aws_sqs_queue_policy`, `aws_lambda_function`,\n`aws_lambda_event_source_mapping` | Queue\npolicies, dead-letter queues, timeouts |\n| Apps | `aws_ecs_service`,\n`aws_ecs_task_definition` | Image tags,\n`ignore_changes` |\n| Databases | `aws_db_instance` |\n`deletion_protection`, `engine_version`,\npassword source |\n| Network | `aws_security_group`,\n`aws_vpc_security_group_ingress_rule` | Inline\nrules or separate rule resources |\n\n`data.aws_iam_policy_document` builds policy\nJSON from HCL blocks. It gives stable JSON, so\nwhitespace or key order cannot cause diffs.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-e6d94c072290",
      "originalText": "What You Will See\n| Area | Resources | What to check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Data buckets | `aws_s3_bucket`, `aws_s3_bucket_versioning`, `aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration`, `aws_s3_bucket_policy`, `aws_s3_bucket_notification`, `aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block` | `force_destroy`, versioning, expiry rules, one notification resource per bucket |\n| Access | `aws_iam_role`, `aws_iam_policy`, `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment`, `data.aws_iam_policy_document` | Trust principals and external IDs, adders or owners |\n| Users with keys | `aws_iam_user`, `aws_iam_access_key` | Where the secret key goes |\n| Secrets | `aws_secretsmanager_secret`, `aws_secretsmanager_secret_version` | Value source, recovery window, `prevent_destroy` |\n| Events | `aws_sns_topic`, `aws_sqs_queue`, `aws_sqs_queue_policy`, `aws_lambda_function`, `aws_lambda_event_source_mapping` | Queue policies, dead-letter queues, timeouts |\n| Apps | `aws_ecs_service`, `aws_ecs_task_definition` | Image tags, `ignore_changes` |\n| Databases | `aws_db_instance` | `deletion_protection`, `engine_version`, password source |\n| Network | `aws_security_group`, `aws_vpc_security_group_ingress_rule` | Inline rules or separate rule resources |\n\n`data.aws_iam_policy_document` builds policy JSON from HCL blocks. It gives stable JSON, so whitespace or key order cannot cause diffs.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "aws-what-you-will-see"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
