    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 6685608329,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-93d00a7a1fe5",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1321.2,
      "y": 2200.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 577.5,
      "seed": 255395,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Where to Look First\nRead an AWS configuration in this order:\n\n1. The `terraform` block: the backend, its key\nand its lock setting, and the version of\n`hashicorp/aws`. A committed\n`.terraform.lock.hcl` tells you the exact\nbuild.\n2. Every `provider \"aws\"` block: the region,\nthe `assume_role` role ARN, aliases,\n`allowed_account_ids` and `default_tags`.\nTogether they tell you where each resource\nlands.\n3. The inputs per environment: workspaces,\nvariable files or YAML files. The same code\ncan run in several accounts.\n4. IAM: the trust policies, the external IDs,\nthe attachment style, and every IAM user with\nan access key.\n5. The data buckets: `force_destroy`,\nversioning, expiry, notifications and\npolicies. Data loss and event wiring live\nhere.\n6. The secrets: where each value comes from,\nthe recovery window and `prevent_destroy`.\n7. The `lifecycle` blocks, and the `moved`,\n`removed` and `import` blocks. They show what\nTerraform will not touch and what moved.\n8. The event paths: queue and topic policies,\ndead-letter queues, and Lambda timeouts.\n9. The lookups of other states, such as data\nsources by name or tag, and SSM parameters.\nThey are the contracts between configurations.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-93d00a7a1fe5",
      "originalText": "Where to Look First\nRead an AWS configuration in this order:\n\n1. The `terraform` block: the backend, its key and its lock setting, and the version of `hashicorp/aws`. A committed `.terraform.lock.hcl` tells you the exact build.\n2. Every `provider \"aws\"` block: the region, the `assume_role` role ARN, aliases, `allowed_account_ids` and `default_tags`. Together they tell you where each resource lands.\n3. The inputs per environment: workspaces, variable files or YAML files. The same code can run in several accounts.\n4. IAM: the trust policies, the external IDs, the attachment style, and every IAM user with an access key.\n5. The data buckets: `force_destroy`, versioning, expiry, notifications and policies. Data loss and event wiring live here.\n6. The secrets: where each value comes from, the recovery window and `prevent_destroy`.\n7. The `lifecycle` blocks, and the `moved`, `removed` and `import` blocks. They show what Terraform will not touch and what moved.\n8. The event paths: queue and topic policies, dead-letter queues, and Lambda timeouts.\n9. The lookups of other states, such as data sources by name or tag, and SSM parameters. They are the contracts between configurations.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "aws-where-to-look-first"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
