      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "One Notification Configuration per Bucket\n`aws_s3_bucket_notification` writes the whole\nnotification configuration of a bucket, so a\nbucket can have only one such resource\n([notification note](https://github.com/hashic\norp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/websit\ne/docs/r/s3_bucket_notification.html.markdown#\nL13)). A second resource, a console edit, or a\nSnowflake pipe with auto-ingest overwrites the\nothers. S3 also rejects two rules with\noverlapping prefixes or suffixes for the same\nevent type ([event filters](https://docs.aws.a\nmazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/notificati\non-how-to-filtering.html)). To send one event\nto several readers, send it to one SNS topic\nor to EventBridge, and fan out from there.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-66dbfc785f33",
      "originalText": "One Notification Configuration per Bucket\n`aws_s3_bucket_notification` writes the whole notification configuration of a bucket, so a bucket can have only one such resource ([notification note](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/r/s3_bucket_notification.html.markdown#L13)). A second resource, a console edit, or a Snowflake pipe with auto-ingest overwrites the others. S3 also rejects two rules with overlapping prefixes or suffixes for the same event type ([event filters](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/notification-how-to-filtering.html)). To send one event to several readers, send it to one SNS topic or to EventBridge, and fan out from there.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "one-notification-configuration"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
