      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Queue Timeouts and Policies\nWhen a Lambda function reads an SQS queue, AWS\nadvises a visibility timeout of at least six\ntimes the function timeout ([Lambda with SQS](\nhttps://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/s\nervices-sqs-configure.html)). For example, a\nfunction with a 60-second timeout needs a\nqueue visibility timeout of at least 360\nseconds. With 300 seconds, a slow batch can\nreach a second reader before the first one\nfinishes. Two more traps:\n\n- Creating or updating a queue with a queue\npolicy hangs unless the policy sets `Version =\n\"2012-10-17\"` ([queue note](https://github.com\n/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0\n/website/docs/r/sqs_queue.html.markdown#L13)).\n- A queue policy for SNS or S3 should name the\nsender with the condition `aws:SourceArn`, so\nno other topic or bucket can write to the\nqueue ([confused deputy](https://docs.aws.amaz\non.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/confused-deputy.ht\nml)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-929cb07c2106",
      "originalText": "Queue Timeouts and Policies\nWhen a Lambda function reads an SQS queue, AWS advises a visibility timeout of at least six times the function timeout ([Lambda with SQS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-sqs-configure.html)). For example, a function with a 60-second timeout needs a queue visibility timeout of at least 360 seconds. With 300 seconds, a slow batch can reach a second reader before the first one finishes. Two more traps:\n\n- Creating or updating a queue with a queue policy hangs unless the policy sets `Version = \"2012-10-17\"` ([queue note](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/r/sqs_queue.html.markdown#L13)).\n- A queue policy for SNS or S3 should name the sender with the condition `aws:SourceArn`, so no other topic or bucket can write to the queue ([confused deputy](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/confused-deputy.html)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "queue-timeouts-and-policies"
      }
    },
