      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Secrets in State\nAn access key, a secret value or a database\npassword in the state is readable by anyone\nwho can read the state bucket. A sensitive\nmark only hides the value in plan output.\nThree ways reduce the exposure: write-only\narguments, programs that read secrets at run\ntime by ARN, and roles instead of access keys.\nAn imported access key has no secret in the\nstate at all ([access key doc](https://github.\ncom/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.7\n3.0/website/docs/r/iam_access_key.html.markdow\nn#L122)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-ea15b27ee859",
      "originalText": "Secrets in State\nAn access key, a secret value or a database password in the state is readable by anyone who can read the state bucket. A sensitive mark only hides the value in plan output. Three ways reduce the exposure: write-only arguments, programs that read secrets at run time by ARN, and roles instead of access keys. An imported access key has no secret in the state at all ([access key doc](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/r/iam_access_key.html.markdown#L122)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "secrets-in-state"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
