    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 5639091639,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-f799b5596904",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1915.6,
      "y": 4800.0,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 280.0,
      "seed": 404610,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Deleted Secrets Hold Their Names\nA deleted secret waits in a recovery window,\n30 days by default ([DeleteSecret](https://doc\ns.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/apirefe\nrence/API_DeleteSecret.html)). During that\ntime, a new secret with the same name fails\nwith \"The secret is scheduled for deletion\" ([\nCreateSecret](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secr\netsmanager/latest/apireference/API_CreateSecre\nt.html)). So a rename or a replacement of a\nsecret resource cannot reuse the name at once.\nThe recovery window is also the only way back\nfrom a wrong destroy. `recovery_window_in_days\n= 0` deletes with no recovery.\n`prevent_destroy` stops the destroy in the\nplan.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-f799b5596904",
      "originalText": "Deleted Secrets Hold Their Names\nA deleted secret waits in a recovery window, 30 days by default ([DeleteSecret](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/apireference/API_DeleteSecret.html)). During that time, a new secret with the same name fails with \"The secret is scheduled for deletion\" ([CreateSecret](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/apireference/API_CreateSecret.html)). So a rename or a replacement of a secret resource cannot reuse the name at once. The recovery window is also the only way back from a wrong destroy. `recovery_window_in_days = 0` deletes with no recovery. `prevent_destroy` stops the destroy in the plan.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "deleted-secrets-hold-names"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
