    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 5518030683,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-36b4238078a1",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1321.2,
      "y": 6073.5,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 175.0,
      "seed": 520698,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Roles Instead of Access Keys\nAn IAM user with an access key has a\nlong-lived secret, and Terraform stores it in\nthe state. A role gives temporary credentials,\nand there is no secret to store. AWS\nrecommends temporary credentials for workloads\n([IAM best practices](https://docs.aws.amazon.\ncom/IAM/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html))\n. Use access keys only for a system that\ncannot assume a role, and plan their rotation.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-36b4238078a1",
      "originalText": "Roles Instead of Access Keys\nAn IAM user with an access key has a long-lived secret, and Terraform stores it in the state. A role gives temporary credentials, and there is no secret to store. AWS recommends temporary credentials for workloads ([IAM best practices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html)). Use access keys only for a system that cannot assume a role, and plan their rotation.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "roles-instead-of-access-keys"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 6209804101,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-b785e9a25001",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
